<header><p class="st-kicker">electorate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Electorate of Baden</h1><p class="st-meta">1803 CE – 1806 CE · capital Karlsruhe</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Baden's three years as an electorate, when the Napoleonic settlement doubled its territory and set it on the way to a grand duchy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden">Charles Frederick</a> had united the two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> margraviates in 1771. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichsdeputationshauptschluss">Imperial Recess of 1803</a> he gained the Palatinate's right-bank lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a>, parts of the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Constance</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-basel">Basel</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-speyer">Speyer</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-strasbourg">Strasbourg</a>, and several imperial cities, and was raised to elector.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden">Charles Frederick</a> was a reforming ruler who had abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> in 1783. As elector he integrated the new lands, whose Catholic and Protestant populations had to be combined, with a new administration and courts, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-university">University of Heidelberg</a> was reorganised in 1803. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in the 1805 campaign.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> gained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breisgau">Breisgau</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. In 1806 it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden">Charles Frederick</a> took the title of Grand Duke, forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-duchy-of-baden">Grand Duchy of Baden</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/electorate-of-baden.jpg" alt="Electorate of Baden" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_Baden_(3%5E2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1803 CE – 1806 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>electorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Karlsruhe</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles Frederick</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kurfürstentum Baden</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1804&amp;focus=electorate-of-baden" aria-label="Electorate of Baden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4874 467 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Electorate of Baden lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5194 723L5170 731M5194 723L5191 731M5194 723L5229 694M5194 723L5194 723M5194 723L5216 762M5194 723L5194 714M5194 723L5217 760M5194 723L5214 760M5194 723L5216 756M5194 723L5186 741M5194 723L5184 739M5194 723L5187 743"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5170 731h0M5191 731h0M5229 694h0M5194 723h0M5216 762h0M5194 714h0M5217 760h0M5214 760h0M5216 756h0M5186 741h0M5184 739h0M5187 743h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5194 723h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5194 723h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Karlsruhe. <a href="/atlas?year=1804&amp;focus=electorate-of-baden">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
